{{also|Vibrato}}
==English==
{{swp}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|it|vibrato|g=m}}, past participle of {{m|it|vibrare||to vibrate}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/vɪˈbɹɑːtoʊ/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑːtəʊ|s=2}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-vibrato.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|music}} The musical effect or technique where the pitch or frequency of a note or sound is quickly and repeatedly raised and lowered over a small distance for the duration of that note or sound.
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1959|year_published=1972|author=w:Anthony Burgess|title=Beds in the East|series=The Malayan Trilogy|page=429|passage=He felt his teeth methodically, one after the other, with a '''vibrato''' movement of finger and thumb.}}

